   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Common Pitfalls\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Losing function metadata with decorators** — __name__, __doc__ are lost.\n",
    "   *Fix:* Use `@wraps` from functools.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **Generators exhausting silently** — can only iterate once.\n",
    "   *Fix:* Convert to list if multiple iterations needed, or recreate.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **Forgetting cleanup in context managers** — resources leak.\n",
    "   *Fix:* Use `contextlib.contextmanager` or ensure __exit__ is correct.\n",
    "\n",
    "4. **Singleton thread safety** — multiple threads get different instances.\n",
    "   *Fix:* Add threading.Lock in __new__.\n",
    "\n",
    "5. **Overusing metaclasses** — complex, hard to debug.\n",
    "   *Fix:* Prefer class decorators or __init_subclass__.\n",
    "\n",
    "6. **Tight coupling in ML code** — hard to test and change.\n",
    "   *Fix:* Use dependency injection and interfaces.\n",
    "\n",
    "7. **Not using @wraps in decorators** — breaks introspection and debugging.\n",
    "   *Fix:* Always add `@wraps(func)` to inner wrapper."
   ]
  }
